MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Believe feels like a natural follow-up to Ten Thousand Fists because I want more of Disturbed's heavy grooves and strong vocals.",
    "Mer De Noms and Opiate connect with my recent interest in 10.000 Days through familiar vocals, atmosphere, or Tool's earlier sound. Vol. 3 also fits my interest in heaviness balanced with melody."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's abrasive percussion and stripped-down sound miss the melody and atmosphere I want from heavy music right now.",
    "A Fever You Can't Sweat Out feels too theatrical and pop-oriented for my current mood. God Hates Us All has relevant aggression, but relentless thrash alone is not enough to make it my next choice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy music seems to have been treated as a broad preference for aggression, even though the vocals, melody, and atmosphere determine what I actually choose.",
    "My earlier rock listening seems to carry too much weight when my latest choices make Disturbed and Tool-related albums more compelling today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent move from Ten Thousand Fists to 10.000 Days makes brooding, atmospheric music and familiar vocal connections especially appealing.",
    "An album can fit my overall taste without being something I would choose now: Dysfunction, Meteora, and Faceless appeal, but Believe and the Tool-related albums give me stronger reasons to listen next."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy rock and metal, but only some capture the familiar vocals, melody, and brooding atmosphere I want next."
}
